policy-ac-send-select-name-hash: TPM2_Policy_AC_SendSelect marks nameHash as set

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_Policy_AC_SendSelect): "If
either policySession→cpHash or policySession→nameHash has been previously set,
the TPM shall return `TPM_RC_CPHASH`. Otherwise, policySession→nameHash will be
set to nameHash ≔ H_policyAlg(objectName ∥ authHandleName ∥ acName)", and
TPM2_PolicyNameHash/TPM2_PolicyCpHash/TPM2_PolicyParameters/
TPM2_PolicyTemplate return `TPM_RC_CPHASH` if it is set.

The reference stores the nameHash in session->u1.cpHash but leaves
isNameHashDefined CLEAR, so IsCpHashUnionOccupied() is FALSE afterwards and a
later TPM2_PolicyNameHash (or PolicyCpHash, PolicyParameters, PolicyTemplate)
succeeds and overwrites the nameHash. The patch sets isNameHashDefined.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/AttachedComponent/Policy_AC_SendSelect.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/AttachedComponent/Policy_AC_SendSelect.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/AttachedComponent/Policy_AC_SendSelect.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/AttachedComponent/Policy_AC_SendSelect.c
@@ -44,6 +44,11 @@ TPM2_Policy_AC_SendSelect(Policy_AC_SendSelect_In* in  // IN: input parameter li
 
     //  complete hash
     CryptHashEnd2B(&hashState, &session->u1.cpHash.b);
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // policySession->nameHash is now set (Part 3, TPM2_Policy_AC_SendSelect), so
+    // the cpHash union is occupied (IsCpHashUnionOccupied()) and a later
+    // TPM2_PolicyCpHash/NameHash/Parameters/Template returns TPM_RC_CPHASH.
+    session->attributes.isNameHashDefined = SET;
 
     // update policy hash
     // Old policyDigest size should be the same as the new policyDigest size since
